INT. BRIGHTWAVE SYNERGY SOLUTIONS - OPEN-PLAN FLOOR - MORNING

Standing desks, kombucha taps, a neon sign that reads GOOD VIBES ONLY. In the center of the floor, a bounce house shaped like a giant inflatable castle wobbles under fluorescent light.

TRIP HALVERSEN, 30s, "Chief Happiness Officer," in a vest that says LEAN IN, stands on a cube with a wireless mic. LAKSHMI PILLAI, 30s, a project manager, sits at her desk with a laptop, headphones, and a thousand-yard stare. GUS ABERNETHY, 50s, a senior accountant, stands at the water cooler, holding a paper cone. DEBORAH-LYNN FOSTER, 40s, the VP of People, arranges lanyards on a folding table.

TRIP
(into mic)
Good morning, Brightwavers! Today's wellness initiative: Synergy Jump!

No one moves. Lakshmi turns a page.

TRIP (CONT'D)
Everybody grab a partner and bounce toward your quarterly goals!

GUS
(to the cooler)
I have goals. They're not in a castle.

DEBORAH-LYNN
Gus, participation is a core value.

GUS
Participation is a hostage situation.

LAKSHMI
(not looking up)
Deborah-Lynn, I have a deadline.

DEBORAH-LYNN
Everyone has a deadline, Lakshmi.

TRIP
Great energy! Love the energy!

The castle's blower sputters. A cough of air. One turret sags.

Lakshmi finally pulls off her headphones.

LAKSHMI
Is that structurally sound?

TRIP
It's rated for three hundred pounds.

GUS
Rated by whom?

TRIP
By... the rental company.

A MAN IN A BEIGE SUIT, 50s, no lanyard, no smile, steps out of the elevator carrying a briefcase. He moves through the floor like a shark through kelp. Nobody stops him.

DEBORAH-LYNN
(whispering to Trip)
Who is that?

TRIP
(whispering back)
I thought he was yours.

The man in the beige suit stops at the castle. Looks up at it. Looks at the mic. Looks at Trip.

BEIGE MAN
Mr. Halversen?

TRIP
Halverson. Trip.

BEIGE MAN
Halverson. I'm from the insurance carrier.

The blower sputters again. Another turret sags. Gus sips his water.

DEBORAH-LYNN
We're in the middle of a team-building --

BEIGE MAN
Yes. I can see.

Lakshmi starts typing again, smiling now.

TRIP
Sir, with respect, this is a culture initiative --

BEIGE MAN
My name is Kent. Kent Aldrich-Bowman. And I am here to tell you that your policy lapsed Monday.

Silence. The castle exhales. Nobody speaks.

TRIP
That's... that can't be right.

KENT
Which is why I brought the paperwork.

He opens the briefcase. Takes out a stack of forms, each tabbed with little yellow flags.

DEBORAH-LYNN
(brightly)
Great! We love paperwork! Trip, give Kent a lanyard.

TRIP
(into mic, shaky)
Everyone, please welcome Kent from... Risk.

GUS
(to Lakshmi)
It's a trap.

LAKSHMI
(under her breath)
It's a rental.

The castle's front wall folds inward with a long, sad hiss. Trip, still clutching his mic, topples slowly into the collapsing fabric and vanishes.

KENT
(calmly, to the room)
Please note the time.

DEBORAH-LYNN
It's 9:14.

KENT
Thank you. 9:14.

He writes it on a form.

LAKSHMI
Does that cover the kombucha?

KENT
Nothing covers the kombucha.

Gus raises his paper cone, solemn, as to a toast.

GUS
To synergy.
